{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovCorner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovCorner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlNormalisation","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalNodeForm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_markov_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_markov_corner","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L191-L313","doc":"**The corner identity at general level `r`.**\n\nFor every removable corner `c` of `ν`,\n\n`∑_{s addable} w_{ν+s} · a(axialDistance c s) = z_r · w_ν`,  `z_r = Q^r/(q·[r]_Q)`, `Q = q²`.\n\nThis is the hypothesis `MarkovAssembly.markov_of_corner_identity` consumes, so with it the Markov\ncondition holds for `wenzlWeight r (q²)` at every integer level — `OcneanuWeightMarkovCorner`'s\nrow-by-row `r = 2` argument, replaced by one uniform proof.\n\nAt `r = 2` the parameter is `q⁴/(q(1+q²)) = q³/(q²+1) = z_D`.\n\nThe proof: the subtype sum becomes a guarded row sum (`sum_addable_eq_sum_range`), which is trimmed\nto `range r` (rows past `colLen 0` are not addable; rows past `r` give a diagram with too many rows,\nwhich `wenzlWeight_addCell_beyond_eq_zero` kills), and each surviving `seminormalParam` becomes the\nnode weight by `axialDistance_corner_addable` + `seminormalParam_node_form`.  Then\n`sum_wenzlWeight_node_weighted` does the arithmetic.\n\nNote there is **no `a = b` special case**: at `s.1 = c.1` the axial distance is `1` and the node form\ngives `(q − q⁻¹)·Q/(Q−1) = q` on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L175-L188","doc":"**Bridge between the corpus's two `axialDistance`s.**\n\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance` (`HoefsmitRep`, via `cellContent`) and\n`QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance` (via `content`) are the same function under two names —\nboth are `(content of the second) − (content of the first)`.  They are `rfl`-equal, but they are\n*different constants*, so a bare `axialDistance` inside `namespace QOU.SchurWeyl` resolves to the\nfirst even under `open QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent`, and a `rw` with a lemma stated in the second\nwill not fire.  `markov_of_corner_identity` uses the first; `axialDistance_corner_addable` the\nsecond.  This lemma is what lets one consume the other.\n\n(The duplication itself is a notation collision worth draining corpus-wide; that is not this file's\nscope.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_wenzlWeight_node_weighted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_wenzlWeight_node_weighted","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L116-L173","doc":"**The algebraic core of the corner identity.**\n\nSumming the branching ratio against the node weight `Q·x_a/(Q·x_a − x_b)` collapses by\n`sum_prod_qratio_weighted` — the Lagrange residue sum — to `Q^r/(Q−1)`, and the branching itself\ncontributes `w_ν/[r]_Q`.  Non-addable rows drop out on their own: the `q`-ratio numerator already\nvanishes there.\n\n`hgap` is the `0/0` guard, supplied at the corner node by `betaR_succ_ne_of_corner`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_succ_ne_of_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_succ_ne_of_corner","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L87-L114","doc":"**No β sits one above a corner's β.**\n\nIf `c` is a removable corner in row `b` then `ν_{b+1} < ν_b`, so `β_{b+1} ≤ β_b − 2`; rows further\ndown are lower still, and rows above have `β > β_b` outright.  Hence `β_i + 1 = β_b` for no `i ≠ b`.\n\nThis is the mirror of `betaR_ne_succ_of_addable`, and it is what discharges the `hne` hypothesis of\n`QOU.Mathlib.sum_prod_qratio_weighted` at the corner node. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.levelBracket_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.levelBracket_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L78-L83","doc":"`[r]_Q ≠ 0` for `r ≠ 0`: it divides `1 − Q^r`, which `hgen` keeps nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.pow_ne_pow_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.pow_ne_pow_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovCorner.lean#L63-L76","doc":"**Distinct exponents give distinct powers** at a non-root-of-unity `Q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}